* A whole number in binary. The bits come out last first, so they are
* kept in an indexed letter and typed from the top down.
1.1 Set b(k) = n - 2·ip(n/2).
1.2 Set n = ip(n/2).
1.3 Set k = k+1.
1.4 To step 1.1 if n > 0.

2.1 Type b(i) in form 1.
Form 1:
_

Set n = 1965.
Set k = 0.
Do part 1.
Do part 2 for i = k-1(-1)0.
